<title>USA: Galoob Toys Inc Q4 net, diluted shr fall.</title>
<headline>Galoob Toys Inc Q4 net, diluted shr fall.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH SAN FRANCISCO, Calif. 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			    Three Months Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>					Dec. 31		 Dec. 31</p>
<p>				    1996	1995	1996     1995</p>
<p> Net revenues		$109,635  $82,966  $284,905 $220,044</p>
<p> Costs of products sold    50,411   38,035   144,282  121,742</p>
<p> Gross margin		  59,224   44,931   140,623   98,302</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>Advertising and</p>
<p>   promotion		   20,038   13,501    43,515   31,240</p>
<p>Other selling and</p>
<p>   administrative	    12,860   11,722    35,776   29,860</p>
<p>Royalties, research and</p>
<p>   development		 12,069    7,442    37,668   24,213</p>
<p> Total operating expenses  44,967   32,665   116,959   85,313</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) from</p>
<p>  operations		   14,257   12,266    23,664   12,989</p>
<p> Interest expense	     (518)  (1,072)   (3,183)  (3,429)</p>
<p> Other income (expense), net  270	226	 455	439</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) before</p>
<p>  income taxes		 14,009   11,420    20,936    9,999</p>
<p>Provision for income taxes</p>
<p>				    1,099	600     2,485	600</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss)	 12,910   10,820    18,451    9,399</p>
<p> Preferred stock dividends     --	782	  21    3,127</p>
<p>Charge related to the</p>
<p>exchange of preferred</p>
<p>  stock for common		 --	 --    24,279	 --</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss)</p>
<p>applicable to common</p>
<p>  shares			 12,910   10,038  ( 5,849)    6,272</p>
<p> Average shares		17,512   10,756    14,289   10,451</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss) per</p>
<p>  common share - primary     0.74     0.93   ( 0.41)     0.60</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss) per</p>
<p>common share - fully</p>
<p>  diluted			  0.74     0.76   ( 0.41)     0.60</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss) per common</p>
<p>excluding charge for exchange</p>
<p>  of preferred stock for common		    1.20	0.60</p>
<p>NOTE (1) In Q1 1996, company offered to exchange 1.85 common shares for each Depositary Convertible Exchangeable Preferred Share outstanding. Offer accepted by 98% of the shares, resulting in issuance of 3,336,433 common shares. GAAP require non-cash charge to reduce Net Earnings Applicable to Common Shares in the EPS calculation for the fair value of the securities issued in excess of the existing rate of approximately 1.185 common shares.  </p>
<p>(2) To improve matching of costs and revenues, company has revised timing of its amortization of tooling, packaging design and sample costs. Effective January 1, these costs are now being amortized on a percentage of annual sales basis rather than previous straight line basis. Change cut Q4 1996 net earnings per common share by $0.05. The change had no impact on full year results.</p>
<p>(3) Certain amounts in 1995 reclassified to conform with the current year's presentation.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
